      "text": "METROBASE Traffic Update as of 5:15pm\n\nWHEN: January 17, 2026\n\nA. MAJOR ROADS:\n\n*EDSA\nSOUTHBOUND \n- Munoz to Bansalangin, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles)\n- Santolan to Connecticut, moderate (due to volume of vehicles) \n- Estrella to Buendia, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles) \n- Magallanes to Taft Ave., slow moving (due to volume of vehicles and DPWH Roadworks at Taft Ave.)\n\nNORTHBOUND\n- FB Harrison to Taft Ave., moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles)\n- Ayala to Buendia, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles) \n- Pioneer to Ortigas, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles) \n- Whiteplains to Aurora blvd, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles)\n- Trinoma to  Quezon City Academy, slow moving (due to volume of vehicles)\n- Kaingin to Balintawak, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles) \n\n*C5\nSOUTHBOUND\n- Magsaysay to UP Town Center, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles) \n- Eastwood to Greenmeadows, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles)\n- Lanuza, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles) \n- Market market to Palar, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles) \n\nNORTHBOUND:\n- Heritage to Palar, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles) \n- Lanuza, moderate (due to volume of vehicles)\n- Greenmeadows to Calle Industria, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles)\n- Bonny Serrano, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles)\n- Aurora Katipunan to Ateneo, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles) \n- UP Town Center, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles) \n\n*COMMONWEALTH\nEASTBOUND:\n- Batasan, moderate (due to volume of vehicles) \n- Manggahan, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles) \n- Doña Carmen to FCM Regalado, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles) \n\nWESTBOUND:\n- Light traffic\n\n*QUEZON AVENUE\nEASTBOUND:\n- Maxima, moderate (due to volume of vehicles) \n- Sct. Borromeo to EDSA, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles) \n\nWESTBOUND:\n- Delta, moderate (due to volume of vehicles) \n- FPJ Ave. to Araneta, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles)\n\n*MARCOS HIGHWAY\nEASTBOUND:\n- SM Marikina to F. Mariano, slow moving (due to volume of vehicles)\n- Sta. Lucia, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles) \n\nWESTBOUND:\n- Town & Country to F. Mariano, slow moving (due to volume of vehicles) \n- Feliz, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles) \n\n*ORTIGAS AVENUE\nEASTBOUND:\n- Greenhills, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles) \n- EDSA to Meralco, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles)\n\nWESTBOUND\n- Greennmeadows to Meralco, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles)\n- EDSA, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles) \n- Greenhills to Santolan, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles)\n\n*ROXAS BOULEVARD\nSOUTHBOUND:\n- Katigbak to Kalaw, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles) \n- Quirino to P. Ocampo, moderate (due to volume of vehicles)\n- Coastal, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles)\n\nNORTHBOUND:\n- Padre Faura to Padre Burgos, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles)\n\n*TAFT AVENUE\nSOUTHBOUND:\n- P. Burgos to UN Ave., moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles)  \n- Quirino, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles) \n- Buendia, moderate (due to volume of vehicles) \n\nNORTHBOUND:\n- Arnaiz, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles) \n- P. Ocampo, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles) \n- UN Ave. to P. Burgos, moderate to slow moving (due to volume of vehicles) \n\n#mmda",
